// A player's name on wrela: a title, a made-up noun and an epithet, all from the lists below
// ("Sir Wobblesnout the Unhurried"). Nobody types a name: the console's server draws one at
// random when an account is made, and the player is knighted with it (a few draws again before
// it is fixed). So no name can say anything a person wrote, and none holds a real name: a name is
// four numbers into these lists, in the picture book's tone (games/capybara/design.md, "Accounts
// and leaderboards"; docs/toolchain-gaps.md has none: this is a choice, not a limit).
//
// The lists are curated by hand. Their test checks every noun the halves can make, every title
// and every epithet against a list of stems a name must never hold, and that no two choices give
// the same text, so a name is unique when its four numbers are (the server keeps them unique).

use std::serialize::Serialize

/// A name: an index into each list.
pub struct Name: Copy + Eq + Serialize {
    pub title: u32,
    pub front: u32,
    pub back: u32,
    pub epithet: u32,
}

